{
  "title": "23: al-Momenoon المؤمنون",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(1)\nQAD AFLAHA MOAMENOONA.\nThe believers must (eventually) win through, \nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(2)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE SALAATEHIM KHAASHEU’OONA.\nThose who humble themselves in their prayers; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُوْنَۙ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’NIL AL-LAGHWE MUA’REZOONA.\nWho avoid vain talk; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِلزَّكٰوةِ فَاعِلُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LELZZAKAAWTE FAAE’ELOONA.\nWho are active in deeds of charity; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِفُرُوْجِهِمْ حٰفِظُوْنَۙ‏(5)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LEFUROOJEHEM HAAFEZOONA.\nWho abstain from sex, \nاِلَّا عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِهِمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُوْمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(6)\nILLAA A’LAA AZWAAJEHIM AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FA INNAHUM GHAYRO MALOOMEENA.\nExcept with those joined to them in the marriage bond, or (the captives) whom their right hands possess, for (in their case) they are free from blame, \nفَمَنِ ابْتَغٰى وَرَآءَ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْعٰدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(7)\nFAMANE’ ABTAGHAA WARAAA-A ZAA LEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AL-A’AADOONA.\nBut those whose desires exceed those limits are transgressors;- \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِاَمٰنٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُوْنَ ۙ‏(8)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LEAAMAANAATEHEM WAA’AHDEHEM RAAU’OONA.\nThose who faithfully observe their trusts and their covenants; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَوٰتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَ‌ۘ‏(9)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’LAA SALAWTEHEM YUHAAFEZOONA.\nAnd who (strictly) guard their prayers;- \nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُوْنَ ۙ‏(10)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AL-WAARESOONA.\nThese will be the heirs, \nالَّذِيْنَ يَرِثُوْنَ الْفِرْدَوْسَؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(11)\nLAZEENA YARESOONA AL-FERDAWSA HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nWho will inherit Paradise: they will dwell therein (for ever). \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ‌ ۚ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN SULAALATIN MIN TEENIN.\nMan We did create from a quintessence (of clay); \nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰهُ نُطْفَةً فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍ‏(13)\nSUMMA LAW NUTFATAN FEE QARAARIN MMAKEENIN.\nThen We placed him as (a drop of) sperm in a place of rest, firmly fixed; \nثُمَّ خَلَقْنَا النُّطْفَةَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْعَلَقَةَ مُضْغَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْمُضْغَةَ عِظٰمًا فَكَسَوْنَا الْعِظٰمَ لَحْمًا ثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنٰهُ خَلْقًا اٰخَرَ‌ ؕ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنُ الْخٰلِقِيْنَ ؕ‏(14)\nSUMMA KHALAQNAL AN-NUTFATA A’ALAQATAN FA KHALAQNAL AL-A’ALAQATA MUZGHATAN FA KHALAQNAL AL-MUZGHATA E’EZAAMAN FAKASAWNAA AL-E’EZAAMA SUMMA NAKSOOHAA SUMMA AANSHAANAAHU KHALQAN AAKHAR FA TABAARAKAS-MO LAAHO AHSANO AL-KHAALEQEENA.\nThen We made the sperm into a clot of congealed blood; then of that clot We made a (foetus) lump; then we made out of that lump bones and clothed the bones with flesh; then we developed out of it another creature. So blessed be Allah, the best to create! \nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ لَمَيِّتُوْنَؕ‏(15)\nSUMMA INNAKUM BA’DA ZAALEKA LAMAYTOONA.\nAfter that, at length ye will die \nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ تُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(16)\nSUMMA INNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE TUBA’ASOONA.\nAgain, on the Day of Judgment, will ye be raised up. \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعَ طَرَآئِقَ ۖ  وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ الْخَلْقِ غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL FAWQAKUM SAB-A’ TARAAEQA WA MAA KUNNAA A’NIL AL-KHALQE GHAAFELEENA.\nAnd We have made, above you, seven tracts; and We are never unmindful of (our) Creation. \nوَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءًۢ بِقَدَرٍ فَاَسْكَنّٰهُ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ۖ وَاِنَّا عَلٰى ذَهَابٍۢ بِهٖ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(18)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN BEQADARIN FAASKANNAAHU FIL ARZE WA INNAA A’LAA ZAHAABIN BEHI LAQAADEROONA.\nAnd We send down water from the sky according to (due) measure, and We cause it to soak in the soil; and We certainly are able to drain it off (with ease). \nفَاَنْشَاْنَا لَكُمْ بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّ اَعْنَابٍ‌ ۘ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَوَاكِهُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(19)\nFA ANSHAANAA LAKUM BEHI JANNAATIN MIN NAKHEELINW WA AAA’NAABIN LAKUM FEEHAA FAWAAKEHU KASEERATUN WWAMENHAA TAAKULOONA.\nWith it We grow for you gardens of date-palms and vines: in them have ye abundant fruits: and of them ye eat (and have enjoyment), \nوَشَجَرَةً تَخْرُجُ مِنْ طُوْرِ سَيْنَآءَ تَنْۢبُتُ بِالدُّهْنِ وَصِبْغٍ لِّلْاٰكِلِيْنَ‏(20)\nWASHAJARATAN TAKHROJO MIN TOORE SAYNAAA TANBUTU BEALDDUHNE WASEBGHIN LLELAAAKELEENA.\nAlso a tree springing out of Mount Sinai, which produces oil, and relish for those who use it for food. \nوَ اِنَّ لَكُمْ فِى الْاَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً‌   ؕ نُسْقِيْكُمْ مِّمَّا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهَا وَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(21)\nWA INNAL LAKUM FIL AL-AANA’AAME LAE’EBRATAN NUSQEEKUM MIMMAA FEE BUTOONEHAA WA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ KASEERATUN WWAMENHAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd in cattle (too) ye have an instructive example: from within their bodies We produce (milk) for you to drink; there are, in them, (besides), numerous (other) benefits for you; and of their (meat) ye eat; \nوَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَ‏(22)\nMAKTASABAT RABBANAA WA FULKE TUHMALOONA.\nAnd on them, as well as in ships, ye ride. \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI FAQAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH AFALAA TATTAQOON.\n(Further, We sent a long line of prophets for your instruction). We sent Noah to his people: He said, “O my people! worship Allah! Ye have no other god but Him. Will ye not fear (Him)?” \nفَقَالَ الْمَلَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَاَنْزَلَ مَلٰٓئِكَةً  ۖۚ مَّا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِىْۤ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(24)\nFAQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YOREEDO AN YYATAFAZZALA A’LAYKUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LA-ANZALA MALAAA-EKATAN MAA SAMEA’NAA BEHAAZAA FEE AABAAA-ENAL AWWALEEN.\nThe chiefs of the Unbelievers among his people said: “He is no more than a man like yourselves: his wish is to assert his superiority over you: if Allah had wished (to send messengers), He could have sent down angels; never did we hear such a thing (as he says), among our ancestors of old.” \nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلٌۢ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا بِهٖ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(25)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJOLUM BEHI JENNATUN FATARABBASOOA BEHI HATTAA HEEN.\n(And some said): “He is only a man possessed: wait (and have patience) with him for a time.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBE SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOONE.\n(Noah) said: “O my Lord! help me: for that they accuse me of falsehood!” \nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ اَنِ اصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَ وَحْيِنَا فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُ‌ۙ فَاسْلُكْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(27)\nFAAWHAYNAA ELAYHE SAALEHAN ASNAE’E AL-FULKA BEAAA’YUNENAA WA WAHYENAA FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA WAFAARA AT-TANNOORU FAASLUK FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNE NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHE QAWLO MINHUM WA LAA TUKHAATEBNEAA FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\nSo We inspired him (with this message): “Construct the Ark within Our sight and under Our guidance: then when comes Our Command, and the fountains of the earth gush forth, take thou on board pairs of every species, male and female, and thy family- except those of them against whom the Word has already gone forth: And address Me not in favour of the wrong-doers; for they shall be drowned (in the Flood). \nفَاِذَا اسْتَوَيْتَ اَنْتَ وَمَنْ مَّعَكَ عَلَى الْفُلْكِ فَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ نَجّٰٮنَا مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(28)\nFA-EZAA ASTAWAYTA ANTA WA MAN BEMAM A’LAL FULKE FA QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE NAJJAANAA MENAL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when thou hast embarked on the Ark - thou and those with thee, say: “Praise be to Allah, Who has saved us from the people who do wrong.” \nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَنْزِلْنِىْ مُنْزَلًا مُّبٰرَكًا وَّاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QUL RABBIL AANZELNEAA MUNZALAN MMUBAARAKAN WWAANTA KHAYRUR AL-MUNZELEENA.\nAnd say: “O my Lord! enable me to disembark with thy blessing: for Thou art the Best to enable (us) to disembark.” \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ وَّاِنْ كُنَّا لَمُبْتَلِيْنَ‏(30)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL WA KUNNAA LAMUBTALEENA.\nVerily in this there are Signs (for men to understand); (thus) do We try (men). \nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(31)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QARNAN AAKHEREEN.\nThen We raised after them another generation. \nفَاَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(32)\nFA-ARSALNAA FEEHIM RASOOLAM MINHUM SAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nAnd We sent to them a messenger from among themselves, (saying), “Worship Allah! ye have no other god but Him. Will ye not fear (Him)?” \nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَتْرَفْنٰهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يَاْكُلُ مِمَّا تَاْكُلُوْنَ مِنْهُ وَيَشْرَبُ مِمَّا تَشْرَبُوْنَ ۙ‏(33)\nWA QAALA MALA-O MIN QAWMEHE LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE AAKHERATE WAATRAFNAAHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YAAKULU MIMMAA TAAKULOONA MINHO WAYASHRABU MIMMAA TASHRABOONA.\nAnd the chiefs of his people, who disbelieved and denied the Meeting in the Hereafter, and on whom We had bestowed the good things of this life, said: “He is no more than a man like yourselves: he eats of that of which ye eat, and drinks of what ye drink. \nوَلَئِنْ اَطَعْتُمْ بَشَرًا مِّثْلَكُمْ اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nWA LAIN AATAA’TUM BASHARAN MMESLAKUM INNAKUM EZAL LLAKHAASEROONA.\n“If ye obey a man like yourselves, behold, it is certain ye will be lost. \nاَيَعِدُكُمْ اَنَّكُمْ اِذَا مِتُّمْ وَكُنْتُمْ تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا اَنَّكُمْ مُّخْرَجُوْنَ ۙ‏(35)\nAAYAE’EDUKUM ANNAKUM EZAA METTUM WA KUNTUM TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN ANNAKUM MMUKHRAJOONA.\n“Does he promise that when ye die and become dust and bones, ye shall be brought forth (again)? \nهَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ ۙ‏(36)\nHAYHAATA HAYHAATA LEMAKH TOO-A’DOON.\n“Far, very far is that which ye are promised! \nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوْثِيْنَ ۙ‏(37)\nIN HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA NAMOOTU WANAHYAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMABU’OOSEENA.\n“There is nothing but our life in this world! We shall die and we live! But we shall never be raised up again! \nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلُ اۨفْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا وَّمَا نَحْنُ لَهٗ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(38)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJULU TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN WA MAA NAHNO LAHU BE-MOAMENEEN.\n“He is only a man who invents a lie against Allah, but we are not the ones to believe in him!” \nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(39)\nQAALA RABBE SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOONE.\n(The prophet) said: “O my Lord! help me: for that they accuse me of falsehood.” \nقَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيْلٍ لَّيُصْبِحُنَّ نٰدِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(40)\nQAALA A’MMAA QALEELIN LLAYUSBEHUNNA NAADEMEENA.\n(Allah) said: “In but a little while, they are sure to be sorry!” \nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ بِالْحَقِّ فَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ غُثَآءً‌ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(41)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR AS-SAYHATU BIL-HAQQE FAJAA’ALNAAHUM GHOSAAA-AN FABUA’DAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nThen the Blast overtook them with justice, and We made them as rubbish of dead leaves (floating on the stream of Time)! So away with the people who do wrong! \nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قُرُوْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَؕ‏(42)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QOROONAN AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We raised after them other generations. \nمَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَؕ‏(43)\nMAA TASBEQU MIN UMMATIN AAJALAHAA WA MAA YASTAAKHEROONA.\nNo people can hasten their term, nor can they delay (it). \nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا تَتْرَا‌ ؕ كُلَّ مَا جَآءَ اُمَّةً رَّسُوْلُهَا كَذَّبُوْهُ‌ فَاَتْبَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ بَعْضًا وَّجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَحَادِيْثَ‌ ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّقَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(44)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA RUSULANAA TATRAA KULLA MAA JAAA-A UMMATAM RRASOOLUHAA KAZZABOOHU FAATBAA’NAA BA’ZAHUM BA’ZAN WWAJAA’ALNAAHUM AAHAADEESA FABUA’DAN LEQAWMINY LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThen sent We our messengers in succession: every time there came to a people their messenger, they accused him of falsehood: so We made them follow each other (in punishment): We made them as a tale (that is told): So away with a people that will not believe! \nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى وَاَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ ۙ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(45)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA MOOSAA WAAKHAAHU AALO BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nThen We sent Moses and his brother Aaron, with Our Signs and authority manifest, \nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا عٰلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(46)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAEH FAS-TAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN A’AALEENA.\nTo Pharaoh and his Chiefs: But these behaved insolently: they were an arrogant people. \nفَقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لِبَشَرَيْنِ مِثْلِنَا وَقَوْمُهُمَا لَنَا عٰبِدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(47)\nFA-QAALOO A-NOAMENO LEBASHARAYNE MESLENAA WAQAWMUHUMAA LANAA A’ABEDOON.\nThey said: “Shall we believe in two men like ourselves? And their people are subject to us!” \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُمَا فَكَانُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْلَكِيْنَ‏(48)\nFA-KAZZABOOHOMAA FA KAANOO MENAL AL-MUHLAKEENA.\nSo they accused them of falsehood, and they became of those who were destroyed. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd We gave Moses the Book, in order that they might receive guidance. \nوَجَعَلْنَا ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَاُمَّهٗۤ اٰيَةً وَّاٰوَيْنٰهُمَاۤ اِلٰى رَبْوَةٍ ذَاتِ قَرَارٍ وَّمَعِيْنٍ‏(50)\nWA JA-A’LNAA NA MARYAMAL WAAMMAH AAYATAL WWAAWAYNAAHUMAA ELAA RABWATIN ZAATIL QARAARIN WWAMAE’EENIN.\nAnd We made the son of Mary and his mother as a Sign: We gave them both shelter on high ground, affording rest and security and furnished with springs. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرُّسُلُ كُلُوْا مِنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَاعْمَلُوْا صَالِحًا‌ ؕ اِنِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ عَلِيْمٌ ؕ‏(51)\nYAA AYYOHAL ROSOLO KOLOO MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAAA’MALOOA SAALEHAN INNEE BEMAA TA’MALOON A’LEEM.\nO ye messengers! enjoy (all) things good and pure, and work righteousness: for I am well-acquainted with (all) that ye do. \nوَاِنَّ هٰذِهٖۤ اُمَّتُكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّاَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(52)\nWA INNA HAAZEHI AUMMATUKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WWAANAA RABBOKUM FAT-TAQOON.\nAnd verily this Brotherhood of yours is a single Brotherhood, and I am your Lord and Cherisher: therefore fear Me (and no other). \nفَتَقَطَّعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًا‌ ؕ كُلُّ حِزْبٍۢ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(53)\nFATAQATTAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM ZUBURAN KULLO HIZBIM BEMAA LADAYHIM FAREEHOON.\nBut people have cut off their affair (of unity), between them, into sects: each party rejoices in that which is with itself. \nفَذَرْهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَتِهِمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(54)\nFAZARHUM FEE GHAMRATEHEM HATTAA HEEN.\nBut leave them in their confused ignorance for a time. \nاَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّمَا نُمِدُّهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ مَّالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَۙ‏(55)\nAAYAHSABOONA ANNAMAA NUMEDDUHUM BEHI MIN MMAALIN WWABANEENA.\nDo they think that because We have granted them abundance of wealth and sons, \nنُسَارِعُ لَهُمْ فِى الْخَيْرٰتِ‌ ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(56)\nNUSAAREU’U LAHUM FIL AL-KHAYRAATE BAL LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nWe would hasten them on in every good? Nay, they do not understand. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مِّنْ خَشْيَةِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّشْفِقُوْنَۙ‏(57)\nINNAL LAZEENA HUM MIN KHASYATIL RABBEHIM MMUSHFEQOONA.\nVerily those who live in awe for fear of their Lord; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM YOAMENOONA.\nThose who believe in the Signs of their Lord; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ لَا يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(59)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-RABBEHIM LAA YUSHREKOON.\nThose who join not (in worship) partners with their Lord; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْتُوْنَ مَاۤ اٰتَوْا وَّ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَجِلَةٌ اَنَّهُمْ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ رٰجِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(60)\nWAL LAZEENA YOATOONAZ MAA AAATAWA WA QULOOBUHUM WAJELATUN ANNAHUM ELAA RABBEHIM RAAJE-O’ON.\nAnd those who dispense their charity with their hearts full of fear, because they will return to their Lord;- \nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَهُمْ لَهَا سٰبِقُوْنَ‏(61)\nOOLAAA-EKA YUSAAREU’OONA FEE AL-KHAYRAATE WA HUM LAHAA SAABEQOONA.\nIt is these who hasten in every good work, and these who are foremost in them. \nوَلَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا‌ وَلَدَيْنَا كِتٰبٌ يَّنْطِقُ بِالْحَقِّ‌ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA LAA NUKALLEFU NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA WA LADAYNAA KETAABUM YYANTEQU BIL-HAQQE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nOn no soul do We place a burden greater than it can bear: before Us is a record which clearly shows the truth: they will never be wronged. \nبَلْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا وَلَهُمْ اَعْمَالٌ مِّنْ دُوْنِ ذٰلِكَ هُمْ لَهَا عٰمِلُوْنَ‏(63)\nBAL QULOOBUHUM FEE GHAMRATIN MIN HAAZAA WA LAHUM AAA’MAALUN MIN DOONIL ZAALEKA HUM LAHAA A’AMELOON.\nBut their hearts are in confused ignorance of this; and there are, besides that, deeds of theirs, which they will (continue) to do, \nحَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَخَذْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهِمْ بِالْعَذَابِ اِذَا هُمْ يَجْئَرُوْنَؕ‏(64)\nHATTAA EZAA AKHAZNAA MUTRAFEEHEM BE-A’ZAABE EZAA HUM YAJAROONA.\nUntil, when We seize in Punishment those of them who received the good things of this world, behold, they will groan in supplication! \nلَا تَجْئَرُوا الْيَوْمَ‌ اِنَّكُمْ مِّنَّا لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(65)\nLAA TAJAROOA YAWMA INNAKUM MINNAA LAA TUNSAROONA.\n(It will be said): “Groan not in supplication this day: for ye shall certainly not be helped by Us. \nقَدْ كَانَتْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِكُمْ تَنْكِصُوْنَۙ‏(66)\nQAD KAANAT AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA KUNTUM A’LAA AAA’QAABEKUM TANKESOONA.\n“My Signs used to be rehearsed to you, but ye used to turn back on your heels- \nمُسْتَكْبِرِيْنَ ‌ۖ  بِهٖ سٰمِرًا تَهْجُرُوْنَ‏(67)\nMUSTAKBEREENA BEHI SAAMERAN TAHJUROONA.\n“In arrogance: talking nonsense about the (Qur'an), like one telling fables by night.” \nاَفَلَمْ يَدَّبَّرُوا الْقَوْلَ اَمْ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا لَمْ يَاْتِ اٰبَآءَهُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(68)\nA-FALAM YADDABBAROOA QAWLA AM JAAA-AHUM MAA LAM TAKOONOO AAABAAAHUMU AWWALEEN.\nDo they not ponder over the Word (of Allah), or has anything (new) come to them that did not come to their fathers of old? \nاَمْ لَمْ يَعْرِفُوْا رَسُوْلَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nAM LAM YAA’REFOOA RASOOLAHUM FAHUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nOr do they not recognise their Messenger, that they deny him? \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ  ؕ بَلْ جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ لِلْحَقِّ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(70)\nAM YAQOOLOONA BEHI JENNATUN BAL JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE WA AKSAROHUM LIL-HAQQE KAAREHOONA.\nOr do they say, “He is possessed”? Nay, he has brought them the Truth, but most of them hate the Truth. \nوَلَوِ اتَّبَعَ الْحَقُّ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ لَفَسَدَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّ‌ؕ بَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِذِكْرِهِمْ فَهُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِهِمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَؕ‏(71)\nWALAWE TABA-A’L HAQQO AHWAAA-AHUM LAFASADATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL WA MAN FEEHENNA BAL AATAYNAAHUM BEZEKREHEM FAHUM A’N ZEKREHEM MMUA’REZOONA.\nIf the Truth had been in accord with their desires, truly the heavens and the earth, and all beings therein would have been in confusion and corruption! Nay, We have sent them their admonition, but they turn away from their admonition. \nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ خَرْجًا فَخَرٰجُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ‌ ‌ۖ  وَّهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(72)\nAM TASALUHUM KHARJAN FAKHARAAJU RABBEKA KHAYRUL WA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nOr is it that thou askest them for some recompense? But the recompense of thy Lord is best: He is the Best of those who give sustenance. \nوَاِنَّكَ لَتَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(73)\nWA LATADU’OOHUM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nBut verily thou callest them to the Straight Way; \nوَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ عَنِ الصِّرَاطِ لَنٰكِبُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA INNA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE A’NIL AS-SERAATE LANAAKEBOONA.\nAnd verily those who believe not in the Hereafter are deviating from that Way. \nوَلَوْ رَحِمْنٰهُمْ وَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهِمْ مِّنْ ضُرٍّ لَّلَجُّوْا فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA LAW RAHEMNAAHUM WAKASHAFNAA MAA BEHIM MIN ZURRIN LLALAJJOOA FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nIf We had mercy on them and removed the distress which is on them, they would obstinately persist in their transgression, wandering in distraction to and fro. \nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْعَذَابِ فَمَا اسْتَكَانُوْا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُوْنَ‏(76)\nWA LAQAD AAKHAZNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABE FAMAA ASTAKAANOOA LE-RABBEHIM WA MAA YATAZARRAU’OONA.\nWe inflicted Punishment on them, but they humbled not themselves to their Lord, nor do they submissively entreat (Him)!- \nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا ذَا عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدٍ اِذَا هُمْ فِيْهِ مُبْلِسُوْنَ‏(77)\nHATTAA EZAA FATAHNA A’LAYHIM BAABAN ZAL A’ZAABIN BAA-SIN EZAA HUM FEEHE MUBLESOONA.\nUntil We open on them a gate leading to a severe Punishment: then Lo! they will be plunged in despair therein! \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ‌  ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AANSHAA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA ABSAARA WAL QALEELAA MAA TASHKOROON.\nIt is He Who has created for you (the faculties of) hearing, sight, feeling and understanding: little thanks it is ye give! \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ ذَرَاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(79)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ZARA-AKUM FIL ARZE WA ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nAnd He has multiplied you through the earth, and to Him shall ye be gathered back. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ وَلَهُ اخْتِلَافُ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEETO LAHUL AKHTELAAFU LAYLE WA WA AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nIt is He Who gives life and death, and to Him (is due) the alternation of Night and Day: will ye not then understand? \nبَلْ قَالُوْا مِثْلَ مَا قَالَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(81)\nBAL QAALOO MISLA MAA QAALA AWWALOON.\nOn the contrary they say things similar to what the ancients said. \nقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّ عِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ‏(82)\nQAALOO A-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’EZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON.\nThey say: “What! when we die and become dust and bones, could we really be raised up again? \nلَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا نَحْنُ وَاٰبَآؤُنَا هٰذَا مِنْ قَبْلُ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(83)\nLAQAD WO-I’DNAA NAHNO WA AABAAA-ONAA HAAZAA MIN QABLO IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\n“Such things have been promised to us and to our fathers before! they are nothing but tales of the ancients!” \nقُلْ لِّمَنِ الْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(84)\nQUL LLEMANE ARZO WA MAN FEEHAA IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay: “To whom belong the earth and all beings therein? (say) if ye know!” \nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(85)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThey will say, “To Allah!” say: “Yet will ye not receive admonition?” \nقُلْ مَنْ رَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(86)\nQUL MAN RRABBU SAMAAWAATE AS-SABE’E WA RABBO A’RSHIL A’ZEEM.\nSay: “Who is the Lord of the seven heavens, and the Lord of the Throne (of Glory) Supreme?” \nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(87)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nThey will say, “(They belong) to Allah.” Say: “Will ye not then be filled with awe?” \nقُلْ مَنْۢ بِيَدِهٖ مَلَكُوْتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ يُجِيْرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(88)\nQUL MAN BE-YADEHI MALAKOOTO KULLE SHAY-IN WA YUJEERU WA LAA YUJAARU A’LAYHE IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay: “Who is it in whose hands is the governance of all things, who protects (all), but is not protected (of any)? (say) if ye know.” \nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ فَاَنّٰى تُسْحَرُوْنَ‏(89)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL FA-ANNAA TUSHAROONA.\nThey will say, “(It belongs) to Allah.” Say: “Then how are ye deluded?” \nبَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(90)\nBAL AATAYNAAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nWe have sent them the Truth: but they indeed practise falsehood! \nمَا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ وَّمَا كَانَ مَعَهٗ مِنْ اِلٰهٍ‌ اِذًا لَّذَهَبَ كُلُّ اِلٰهٍۢ بِمَا خَلَقَ وَلَعَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ‌ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(91)\nMAA TAKHAZA LAAHO MIN WWALADIN WA MAA KAANA MA-A’HU MIN ELAAHIN EZAL LLAZAHABA KULLO ELAAHIN BEMAA KHALAQAL WALAA’ALAA KHALAA A’LAA BA’Z WA LAAHE LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nNo son did Allah beget, nor is there any god along with Him: (if there were many gods), behold, each god would have taken away what he had created, and some would have lorded it over others! Glory to Allah! (He is free) from the (sort of) things they attribute to Him! \nعٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(92)\nA’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FATAA’AALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nHe knows what is hidden and what is open: too high is He for the partners they attribute to Him! \nقُل رَّبِّ اِمَّا تُرِيَنِّىْ مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(93)\nQUL RABBIL IMMAA TUREENNEAA MAA YOOA’ADOONA.\nSay: “O my Lord! if Thou wilt show me (in my lifetime) that which they are warned against, \nرَبِّ فَلَا تَجْعَلْنِىْ فِى الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(94)\nRABBE FALAA TAJA’ALNEAA FIL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\n“Then, O my Lord! put me not amongst the people who do wrong!” \nوَاِنَّا عَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّرِيَكَ مَا نَعِدُهُمْ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA INNAA A’LAA AN NNUREEKA MAA NAE’EDUHUM LAQAADEROONA.\nAnd We are certainly able to show thee (in fulfilment) that against which they are warned. \nاِدْفَعْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ السَّيِّئَةَ‌ ؕ نَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(96)\nBILLATEE BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO SAYYEATE NAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASEFOONA.\nRepel evil with that which is best: We are well acquainted with the things they say. \nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَمَزٰتِ الشَّيٰطِيْنِۙ‏(97)\nWA QUL RABBIL A-OO’ZO BEKA MIN HAMAZAATE ASH-SHAYTEENE.\nAnd say “O my Lord! I seek refuge with Thee from the suggestions of the Evil Ones. \nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ رَبِّ اَنْ يَّحْضُرُوْنِ‏(98)\nWA A-OO’ZO BEKA RABBE AN YYAHZUROONE.\n“And I seek refuge with Thee O my Lord! lest they should come near me.” \nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَ اَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ارْجِعُوْنِۙ‏(99)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AAHADAHUMU MAWTO QAALA RABBE ARJEU’OONE.\n(In Falsehood will they be) Until, when death comes to one of them, he says: “O my Lord! send me back (to life), \nلَعَلِّىْۤ اَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيْمَا تَرَكْتُ‌ؕ كَلَّا‌ ؕ اِنَّهَا كَلِمَةٌ هُوَ قَآئِلُهَا‌ؕ وَمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ بَرْزَخٌ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(100)\nLAA’ALLEAA AAA’MALU SAALEHAN FEEMAA TARAKTU KALLAA INNAHAA KALEMATUN HOWA QAAELUHAA WA MIN WA-RAAA-EHIM BARZAKHUL ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\n“In order that I may work righteousness in the things I neglected.” - “By no means! It is but a word he says.”- Before them is a Partition till the Day they are raised up. \nفَاِذَا نُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَلَاۤ اَنْسَابَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَّلَا يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(101)\nFA-EZAA NUFEKHA FIL SOORE FALAA AANSAABA BAYNAHUM YAWMA-EZIN WA LAA YATASAAA-ALOON.\nThen when the Trumpet is blown, there will be no more relationships between them that Day, nor will one ask after another! \nفَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(102)\nFAMAN SAQOLAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThen those whose balance (of good deeds) is heavy, they will attain salvation: \nوَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(103)\nWA MAN KHAFFAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FEE JAHANNAMA KHAALEDOON.\nBut those whose balance is light, will be those who have lost their souls, in Hell will they abide. \nتَلْفَحُ وُجُوْهَهُمُ النَّارُ وَهُمْ فِيْهَا كٰلِحُوْنَ‏(104)\nTALFAHU WUJOOHAHUMU TAMASSANAN WA HUM FEEHAA KAALEHOONA.\nThe Fire will burn their faces, and they will therein grin, with their lips displaced. \nاَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(105)\nALAM TAKUN AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\n“Were not My Signs rehearsed to you, and ye did but treat them as falsehood?” \nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتْ عَلَيْنَا شِقْوَتُنَا وَكُنَّا قَوْمًا ضَآلِّيْنَ‏(106)\nQAALOO RABBANAA GHALABAT A’LAYNAA SHEQWATUNAA KUNNAA QAWMAN ZAALLEENA.\nThey will say: “our Lord! Our misfortune overwhelmed us, and we became a people astray! \nرَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا مِنْهَا فَاِنْ عُدْنَا فَاِنَّا ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(107)\nRABBANAA AAKHREJNAA MINHAA FA-IN U’UDNAA FAINNAA ZAALEMOON.\n“Our Lord! bring us out of this: if ever we return (to Evil), then shall we be wrong-doers indeed!” \nقَالَ اخْسَئُوْا فِيْهَا وَلَا تُكَلِّمُوْنِ‏(108)\nQAALA AKHSAOOA FEEHAA WA LAA TUKALLEMOONE.\nHe will say: “Be ye driven into it (with ignominy)! And speak ye not to Me! \nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‌‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(109)\nINNAHU KAANA FAREEQUM MIN E’BAADEE YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAMANNAA FAGH-FIR LANAA HAMNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR AR-RAAHEMEENA.\n“A part of My servants there was, who used to pray 'our Lord! we believe; then do Thou forgive us, and have mercy upon us: For Thou art the Best of those who show mercy!” \nفَاتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا حَتّٰٓى اَنْسَوْكُمْ ذِكْرِىْ وَكُنْتُمْ مِّنْهُمْ تَضْحَكُوْنَ‏(110)\nFAATTAKHAZTUMOOHUM SEKHREEA HATTAA AANSAWKUM ZEKREAA WA KUNTUM MINHUM TAZHAKOONA.\n“But ye treated them with ridicule, so much so that (ridicule of) them made you forget My Message while ye were laughing at them! \nاِنِّىْ جَزَيْتُهُمُ الْيَوْمَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْۤا ۙ اَنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(111)\nINNEE JAZAYTUHUMU YAWMA BEMAA SABAROO ANNAHUM HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\n“I have rewarded them this Day for their patience and constancy: they are indeed the ones that have achieved Bliss...” \nقٰلَ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ عَدَدَ سِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nQAALA KAM LABISTUM FIL ARZE A’ADADA SENEEN.\nHe will say: “What number of years did ye stay on earth?” \nقَالُوْا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا اَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ فَسْئَلِ الْعَآدِّيْنَ‏(113)\nQAALOO LABESNAA YAWMAN AW YAWM YAWMIN FASALE AL-A’AADDEENA.\nThey will say: “We stayed a day or part of a day: but ask those who keep account.” \nقٰلَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا لَّوْ اَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA IN LLABESTUM ILLAA QALEELAA LAW ANNAKUM KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nHe will say: “Ye stayed not but a little, if ye had only known! \nاَفَحَسِبْتُمْ اَنَّمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ عَبَثًا وَّاَنَّكُمْ اِلَيْنَا لَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(115)\nAFAHASIBTUM ANNAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM A’BASANW WA ANNAKUM ELAYNAA LAA TURJAO’ON. \n“Did ye then think that We had created you in jest, and that ye would not be brought back to Us (for account)?” \nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ۚ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ‏(116)\nFA-TAA’ALAL LAAHUL MALEKUL HAQQO, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL KAREEM. \nTherefore exalted be Allah, the King, the Reality: there is no god but He, the Lord of the Throne of Honour! \nوَمَنْ يَّدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَۙ لَا بُرْهَانَ لَهٗ بِهٖۙ فَاِنَّمَا حِسَابُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MANY YAD-O’ MA-A’LLAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA, LAA BURHAANA LAHU BEHI, FA-INNAMAA HESAABOHU I’NDA RABBEHI, INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUL KAAFEROON. \nIf anyone invokes, besides Allah, Any other god, he has no authority therefor; and his reckoning will be only with his Lord! and verily the Unbelievers will fail to win through! \nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(118)\nWA QUR RABBIGH FIR WAR HAM WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAHEMEEN.\nSo say: “O my Lord! grant Thou forgiveness and mercy for Thou art the Best of those who show mercy!” ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Momenoon (The Believers)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 118 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reciter of this Surah will feel great comfort when the angel of death comes to take his soul and he will be given the good news of his position by angels.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah on every Friday, he will have a great status in the hereafter and will be in the company of prophets. If this Surah is written (at night) and put on the neck of a drunkard, he will start hating intoxicating drinks and will stop this bad habit."
}
